256:- **Checks before Prescribe:** daily schedule with no dose at all → "Choose a dose for at least one time of day." · Other picked with no valid number → "Enter the dose in ml/units." or "Use numbers only, e.g. 7.5 units." (only plain positive numbers: 7, 7.5, .5).
257:- **An error on Prescribe scrolls the screen to the first error.** The M / A / N "choose a dose" error is field text under the grid, not a tinted box; other errors sit under their field (D-81 F16).
258:- **Prescribe** saves, marks the medicine Prescribed (and re-enables it if it was disabled).
263:**Printed line** = schedule · duration · food (if chosen) · instructions (if written), e.g. "1-0-1 + SOS 1 tablet (max 1 tablet/day) · 6 months · After food". **SOS limit (D-80 pt 3, D-81 F14):** the daily total in the medicine's unit: "2 puffs as needed (max 8 puffs/day)"; a total of 1 is singular ("max 1 tablet/day"); cream prints "Apply as needed (max 3 times/day)".
267:## 9. Order details, Rx viewer, notes
268:- **Keyboard rule (D-81):** on Prescribe (Other dose, Additional instructions) and the case page (Chief complaints, Doctor notes) the focused field scrolls into view above the keyboard with its label and helper. The pinned action bar hides while the keyboard is open and returns when it closes (same reason as D-43).
